        <h2 class="section-heading">Degree Requirements</h2>
        <p>The MLIS program consists of 39 credit hours, including 19 credits of required courses (https://cloud.mizzou.edu/mlis-MLIS-Spring2023-Later). Elective courses are selected in consultation with faculty advisors.</p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
            <li class="list-item">Must include 15 credit hours at or above the 8000 level.</li>
            <li class="list-item">Must include 12 hours of courses taught by a full-time faculty member.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Classes are 100% online, but some classes have a synchronous (real-time interaction) component. Course registration materials will indicate whether a course has synchronous sessions and, if so, the meeting times.</p>

        <h2 class="section-heading">For additional information about planning your Program of Study, see the LIS Student Resources (https://cloud.mizzou.edu/information-science/lis-student-resources/). Consult the MLIS Program Handbook for detailed degree requirements and program information (https://cloud.mizzou.edu/mlis-program-handbook/).</h2>

